// Secrets.xcconfig.example — committed. Copy to `Secrets.xcconfig` (gitignored)
// and fill in real values. Every key *declared* here must exist in both files;
// the example is the only record of what a new machine or CI job has to supply.
// A key left commented out here is documentation of one you may add later — it
// is permitted in your copy, never required.
//
// `//` starts a comment in xcconfig, so a URL's scheme separator must be
// written as `https:/$()/host` — the `$()` expands to nothing at build time.
// Write `https://host` and the value silently truncates to `https:`.
//
// Quoting does NOT help, and this is the mistake worth naming: xcconfig has no
// string literals and no escape character. Quotes are ordinary characters, so
// "https://host" truncates the same way and leaves a stray quote behind, and
// \/\/ survives the comment marker only by putting literal backslashes in the
// value. A trailing comment on the same line as a URL fails too — the first //
// wins, and that's the one inside the URL. `$()` (or `${}`) is the only escape
// there is. All of this is verified against `xcodebuild -showBuildSettings`.
//
// A key left blank here is not a soft default: `$(KEY)` expands to an empty
// string, and on a networked project the composition root stops the app at
// launch rather than let it run against a wrong-but-plausible URL. Run
// `Scripts/check_secrets.sh` to catch an empty or truncated value at commit
// time instead of in the simulator.

// Per-configuration base URL. RequestBuilder's `baseURL` comes from here via
// the composition root — never a literal URL inside a Service (§3.7, §8.3).
API_BASE_URL = https:/$()/api.staging.example.com

// A key that must ship in the binary is public: it is extractable from the IPA.
// Add one here only when the vendor's threat model allows a client-side key;
// anything genuinely sensitive stays server-side behind your own endpoint.
//
// Nothing reads this yet — a client key follows the same path as API_BASE_URL:
// add it to the app target's Info.plist via $(API_KEY), read it in the
// composition root, and pass it into RequestBuilder's defaultHeaders. Uncomment
// only once you've done that wiring, so the file never lists a key that goes
// nowhere.
// API_KEY =
